{
  "_doc": "Seabra (Seabra's Market / Seabra Foods) NJ store locations, geocoded. Feeds the nearest_seabra_mi columns in share/by_town.csv + share/amenities.csv via build_share.py. Store list added 2026-07-13; coordinates from the US Census geocoder (key-less, cloud-safe) the same day.",
  "_intent": "Proximity to a Seabra is a NICE-TO-HAVE for a house, never a requirement. It is reported as a soft signal (distance to the nearest store) and MUST NOT be used to filter, exclude, or rank out a town or a listing. No thresholds.",
  "_coverage_note": "The stores sit OUTSIDE the target towns (Newark/Union/Elizabeth/Kearny/Harrison/Hillside/Old Bridge are not in zips.json) and that is expected \u2014 the question is never 'is there a Seabra in this town' but 'how far is the nearest one'. So this joins by DISTANCE, never by town/zip equality.",
  "_schema": "locations[]: brand, name, town, state, zip, address (as given), lat/lon, geocode_precision ('rooftop' = Census address match | 'zip_centroid' = fallback, ~1 mi slop), geocode_matched (what the geocoder actually resolved to \u2014 check this before trusting a row; e.g. the Old Bridge store resolved to 'STATE RTE 516', which is the same road as 'County Road 516').",
  "_caveats": [
    "Distances are STRAIGHT-LINE (haversine), not drive time. In this part of NJ the drive is typically 1.3-1.5x the crow-flies mileage. Fine for a nice-to-have; do not quote it as a commute.",
    "1 of 11 stores (Elizabeth, 1000 S Elmora Ave) had no Census address point and is placed at its ZCTA centroid \u2014 treat its distance as +/- ~1 mi.",
    "Store list is a point-in-time snapshot, not scraped or refreshed. Stores close and open; re-verify before leaning on it."
  ],
